From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] rs6000: hybrid ILP32 TOC entries for addresses stay 4 bytes at Pmode

With Pmode DImode (0059), a symbol address needed in Pmode (the base of a
load or store of a global) fell through to force_const_mem (Pmode, ...):
an 8-byte .quad TOC entry read with ld.  Only the ptr_mode path (taking
the address as a pointer value) used the 4-byte .long entry and lwz.  Every
-mcmodel=small program's TOC doubled, two entries were kept per symbol
(one of each size), and tests/sdk/large-toc-test.sh's ILP32 control (two
objects, under 64 KiB of TOC before) needed several TOC groups and was
refused by ld.

A Pmode move of a symbolic address that comes from a TOC entry now loads
it in ptr_mode (the same 4-byte entry, lwz) and zero-extends it; pointers
are zero-extended in this ABI, so lwz alone forms the 64-bit address and
combine folds the extension into the load.  Symbols reached TOC-relative
(addis/addi) are formed directly as before: the ptr_mode move sends them
back at Pmode, so they are excluded to keep the two moves from recursing.
TLS references and integer constants are unchanged.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.cc
@@ -11014,6 +11014,37 @@ rs6000_emit_move (rtx dest, rtx source, machine_mode mode)
 	    }
 #endif
 
+	  /* Hybrid ILP32 (Pmode DImode, ptr_mode SImode): an address that
+	     comes from a TOC entry lives in a pointer-sized (4-byte) entry.
+	     Load it in ptr_mode (lwz from the 4-byte slot, the same entry the
+	     ptr_mode move above uses) and zero-extend, rather than giving it
+	     an 8-byte entry read with ld: that doubled the TOC of every
+	     -mcmodel=small program and kept two entries per symbol.  */
+	  rtx toc_base = operands[1];
+	  if (GET_CODE (toc_base) == CONST
+	      && GET_CODE (XEXP (toc_base, 0)) == PLUS)
+	    toc_base = XEXP (XEXP (toc_base, 0), 0);
+	  if (mode == Pmode && ptr_mode != Pmode && TARGET_TOC
+	      && can_create_pseudo_p ()
+	      && (SYMBOL_REF_P (operands[1])
+		  || GET_CODE (operands[1]) == LABEL_REF
+		  || (GET_CODE (operands[1]) == CONST
+		      && !CONST_INT_P (XEXP (operands[1], 0))))
+	      && !tls_referenced_p (operands[1])
+	      /* A TOC-relative base is formed directly (the ptr_mode move
+		 would send it back here at Pmode).  */
+	      && !(SYMBOL_REF_P (toc_base)
+		   && use_toc_relative_ref (toc_base, Pmode)))
+	    {
+	      rtx narrow = gen_reg_rtx (ptr_mode);
+	      rs6000_emit_move (narrow,
+				convert_memory_address (ptr_mode, operands[1]),
+				ptr_mode);
+	      emit_insn (gen_rtx_SET (operands[0],
+				      gen_rtx_ZERO_EXTEND (Pmode, narrow)));
+	      return;
+	    }
+
 	  /* If we are to limit the number of things we put in the TOC and
 	     this is a symbol plus a constant we can add in one insn,
 	     just put the symbol in the TOC and add the constant.  */
